{"hey":{"id":"ec1aa0e9-0587-4a87-a788-9280e53fd65e","word":"hey","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"exclamation to get attention","word":"ei"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"protest or reprimand","word":"ei"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"protest or reprimand","word":"epa"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"protest or reprimand","word":"opa"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"expression of surprise","word":"epa"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"expression of surprise","word":"opa"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"informal greeting","word":"oi"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"informal greeting","word":"e aí"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"request for repetition or explanation","word":"hã"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"request for repetition or explanation","word":"hem"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"meaningless beat marker, filler syllable","word":"é"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"meaningless beat marker, filler syllable","word":"hey"}],"pos":"intj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Hey, look at this!","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"ece18d98-f0d5-45bb-baa7-90b6da91444a"},{"text":"Hey! Listen!","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"ddc553ad-09cb-4b84-9a61-69a6294cc956"}],"links":[["exclamation","exclamation"],["attention","attention"]],"glosses":["An exclamation to get attention."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["informal"],"id":"cf860782-5640-469c-9fbc-6941447dab80"},{"examples":[{"text":"Hey! Stop that!","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"9fe06a98-4988-40d8-8cd5-e92608f24e6b"}],"links":[["protest","protest"],["reprimand","reprimand"]],"glosses":["A protest or reprimand."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["informal"],"id":"60bb7d8d-c70d-47f3-9ff1-725350712145"},{"examples":[{"text":"Hey! This is new!","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"f0aa9711-69ab-4e5e-abb4-ed377cfa7193"}],"links":[["expression","expression"],["surprise","surprise"]],"glosses":["An expression of surprise."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["informal"],"id":"4f333af4-4d32-493a-90b5-348b70de949c"},{"examples":[{"text":"Hey! How's it going?","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"e366100b-8079-4e93-a4c2-b7042068d023"}],"links":[["informal","informal#English"],["greeting","greeting#English"],["hi","hi#English"]],"glosses":["An informal greeting, similar to hi."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["informal"],"id":"5d6df408-6950-4fe8-b0ee-c0a09f71414c"},{"examples":[{"text":"Hey? How's that?","bold_text_offsets":[[0,3]],"type":"example","id":"a603f181-8145-4272-b2ed-ba41d69a07d6"}],"links":[["request","request"],["repetition","repetition"],["explanation","explanation"],["confusion","confusion"]],"glosses":["A request for repetition or explanation; an expression of confusion."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["informal"],"id":"e4c81e91-a8a7-499c-a052-1e3eda262cb5"},{"examples":[{"text":"\"Who 's a cur - now - hey?\"","ref":"1900, Joseph Conrad, Lord Jim, page vi. 54:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[22,25]],"id":"09826e1e-0a60-4aeb-b8a0-3f4426464cd4"}],"links":[["tag question","tag question#English"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Used as a tag question, to emphasise what goes before or to request that the listener express an opinion about what has been said."],"tags":["informal"],"id":"eb0cee07-f361-43cb-9fcd-23ced12bb52b"},{"examples":[{"text":"The chorus is \"nana na na, nana na na hey hey hey, goodbye\".","bold_text_offsets":[[38,49]],"type":"example","id":"44802d3d-f59b-4356-95e3-d561ca2138c0"}],"links":[["beat","beat"],["marker","marker"],["filler","filler"],["syllable","syllable"]],"glosses":["A meaningless beat marker or extra, filler syllable in song lyrics."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["informal"],"id":"8af224af-c5af-4784-ae25-b16cb0175a70"}],"related":[{"word":"huh"},{"word":"hay is for horses"},{"word":"attention","source":"Thesaurus:hey","tags":["noun"]},{"word":"pay attention","source":"Thesaurus:hey","tags":["verb"]}],"synonyms":[{"sense":"exclamation to get attention","word":"oi"},{"word":"yo"},{"sense":"expression of surprise","word":"blimey"},{"word":"gee whiz"},{"word":"yowzah"},{"word":"wow"},{"sense":"for repetition or explanation","word":"eh"},{"sense":"for repetition or explanation","word":"huh"},{"sense":"informal greeting","word":"hi"},{"word":"howdy"},{"word":"wotcher"},{"word":"hello"},{"word":"ahem","source":"Thesaurus:hey"},{"word":"ahoy","source":"Thesaurus:hey","topics":["nautical","transport"]},{"word":"cooee","source":"Thesaurus:hey","tags":["Australia"]},{"word":"hey","source":"Thesaurus:hey"},{"word":"heyo","source":"Thesaurus:hey"},{"word":"hoi","source":"Thesaurus:hey","tags":["Britain"]},{"word":"oi oi","source":"Thesaurus:hey","tags":["British","slang"]},{"word":"yoohoo","source":"Thesaurus:hey"}]},"heyday":{"id":"7843bf3e-c373-449a-8767-9785b310a5fe","word":"heyday","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a period of success, popularity or power","tags":["masculine"],"word":"auge"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The early twentieth century was the heyday of the steam locomotive.","bold_text_offsets":[[36,42]],"type":"example","id":"80044b6d-47c3-4471-9dba-817a9c948de7"},{"text":"Must your hot ytch and plurisie of lust, The heyday of your luxury, be fedd Up to a surfeite, and could none but I Be pickt out to be cloake to your close tricks, Your belly-sports?","ref":"c. 1626 or 1629–1633 (first performance), [John Ford], ’Tis Pitty Shee’s a Whore […], London: […] Nicholas Okes for Richard Collins, […], published 1633, →OCLC, Act IV:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[45,51]],"id":"637da1f2-733b-47b3-a076-f3d8960948b7"},{"text":"She started learning the craft at age 13 from her father, who founded the family's tile business, Kam Fat Mahjong, in 1962. Masters who would visit Hong Kong during its manufacturing heyday in the 1970s and 80s also shared their techniques and trained apprentices.","ref":"2025 July 27, Kathleen Magramo, “The game is almost over for one of Hong Kong’s last mahjong carvers”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[183,189]],"id":"4dd75cd8-ed9c-4fd3-9fd1-dad783479445"},{"text":"There has been a marked shift in viewing habits since the channels’ heyday, with music videos now more commonly consumed on YouTube and social media rather than television.","ref":"2026 January 1, Max Pilley, “MTV shuts down final music-only channels with ‘Video Killed The Radio Star’”, in NME:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[68,74]],"id":"3c2a19f5-ae30-4ee1-9a81-c77f41b8ed70"}],"links":[["period","period"],["success","success"],["popularity","popularity"],["power","power"],["prime","prime"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["A period of success, popularity, or power; prime."],"id":"de3f9417-dcc8-4bd2-92ef-4f4fe40bc290"},{"categories":["English terms with archaic senses"],"links":[["exultation","exultation"],["spirit","spirit"],["gaiety","gaiety"],["frolic","frolic"]],"raw_glosses":["(archaic) An exultation of the spirits; gaiety; frolic."],"glosses":["An exultation of the spirits; gaiety; frolic."],"tags":["archaic"],"id":"31113ad9-ffbe-495b-9d97-d75762312e9b"}],"related":[{"word":"hey"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"day in the sun"},{"word":"golden age"},{"word":"golden years"},{"word":"good old days"}]}}
